{"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarimaparallel"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Discover optimal autoregressive, integrated, and moving average orders across ((p, d, q) \\times (P, D, Q)_s) grids using parallel Swift Concurrency.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAParallel"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Automated-Time-Series","title":"Automated Time Series","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMA","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAOrder","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMACriterion"]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","title":"Guides & Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/ArimaAndSarima","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/SmoothingAndDecomposition","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/KoopmanOperator"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Manually diagnosing autocorrelation functions (ACF) and partial autocorrelation functions (PACF) to select ARIMA orders is time-consuming and error-prone. Standard automated packages like R’s "},{"code":"forecast::auto.arima","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or Python’s "},{"code":"pmdarima","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" search across candidate orders sequentially."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"AutoARIMA","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" evaluates the entire hyperparameter lattice simultaneously across all CPU cores on Apple Silicon using structured Swift Concurrency (","type":"text"},{"code":"withThrowingTaskGroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Grid-Search-Architecture","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Grid Search Architecture"},{"code":["           Observed Time Series [y_1, y_2, ..., y_N]","                               │","       ┌───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┐","       ▼                       ▼                       ▼","ARIMA(1, 1, 0)          ARIMA(2, 1, 1)          ARIMA(0, 1, 2)","Task 1                  Task 2                  Task 3","   │                       │                       │","   ├─ Hannan-Rissanen      ├─ Hannan-Rissanen      ├─ Hannan-Rissanen","   └─ Compute AIC\/BIC      └─ Compute AIC\/BIC      └─ Compute AIC\/BIC","       │                       │                       │","       └───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┘","                               ▼","                withThrowingTaskGroup Collector","                               │","                               ▼","                 Sorted Leaderboard & Best Model"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"anchor":"Information-Criteria","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Information Criteria"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"AIC (Akaike Information Criterion)"}]},{"text":": Penalizes model complexity while rewarding likelihood:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"$$\\text{AIC} = 2k - 2\\ln(L)$$","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"BIC (Bayesian Information Criterion)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Imposes a stronger penalty proportional to sample size:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"$$\\text{BIC} = k\\ln(N) - 2\\ln(L)$$","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Example-Usage","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Example Usage"},{"code":["import SwiftForecast","","\/\/ 1. Initialize AutoARIMA with bounded search ranges","let autoArima = AutoARIMA(","    maxP: 3,","    maxD: 2,","    maxQ: 3,","    criterion: .aic",")","","\/\/ 2. Concurrently fit candidates across all cores","let result = try await autoArima.fit(series: historicalPrices)","print(\"Optimal Order: \\(autoArima.bestOrder!) with AIC: \\(autoArima.bestScore!)\")","","\/\/ 3. Generate multi-step forecasts","let forecast = try await autoArima.forecast(horizon: 12)","print(\"Forecasted points: \\(forecast.forecast.predictions)\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Stability--Convergence-Guarantees","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Stability & Convergence Guarantees"},{"anchor":"Zero-Variance-Degenerate-Inputs","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Zero-Variance Degenerate Inputs"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If an input series is constant or exhibits zero numerical variance ($\\text{var} < 10^{-12}$), standard likelihood optimization can diverge or enter infinite loops. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AutoARIMA"},{"text":" detects zero variance upfront, immediately fitting an exact ARIMA(0, 0, 0) constant model:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Avoids matrix singularities in the Hannan-Rissanen and Yule-Walker algorithms.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Guarantees instant return without stalling the task group."}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Fixed-Iteration-Bound","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Fixed Iteration Bound"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All internal parameter search loops are strictly bounded by a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations = 500"},{"type":"text","text":" ceiling, ensuring that numerical optimization always converges in deterministic time across parallel worker threads."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftForecast"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Concurrent Order Selection with AutoARIMA"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"references":{"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast":{"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast","title":"SwiftForecast","abstract":[{"text":"Time Series & Volatility Forecasting Models.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/ArimaAndSarima":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Forecast univariate time series using Autoregressive Integrated Moving Average (ARIMA) and Seasonal ARIMA (SARIMA)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/ArimaAndSarima","title":"ARIMA & SARIMA Time Series Models","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/arimaandsarima"},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/AutoARIMACriterion":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMACriterion","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarimacriterion","title":"AutoARIMACriterion","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AutoARIMACriterion"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AutoARIMACriterion"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Information criterion utilized for model selection in ","type":"text"},{"code":"AutoARIMA","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/AutoARIMAOrder":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A structure identifying the selected ARIMA \/ SARIMA order.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AutoARIMAOrder"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAOrder","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarimaorder","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AutoARIMAOrder","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"AutoARIMAOrder","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/AutoARIMA":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AutoARIMA"}],"title":"AutoARIMA","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMA","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Automated hyperparameter grid search for ARIMA and SARIMA time-series models."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarima","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AutoARIMA","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/SmoothingAndDecomposition":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Model trends, seasonality, volatility, and dynamic state transitions using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ExponentialSmoothing"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NelderMead"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KalmanFilter"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GARCHModel"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeSeriesDecomposition"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Time Series Forecasting, Smoothing & Kalman Filtering","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/SmoothingAndDecomposition","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/smoothinganddecomposition"},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/KoopmanOperator":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/koopmanoperator","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Koopman Operator time-series forecasting and dynamical system modeling actor.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Uses Extended Dynamic Mode Decomposition (EDMD) to approximate non-linear dynamics","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"via linear operators in lifted observable feature spaces.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"KoopmanOperator","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"KoopmanOperator","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/KoopmanOperator","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"KoopmanOperator"}]}}}